        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-24" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#36393d;fillColor=#cce5ff;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;find critical path quickly, bring teams together, folloup the actions and keep stakholder fully update&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="92" width="186" x="407" y="2081" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-25" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffff88;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Objective&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="171" x="79" y="1909" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-26" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#cdeb8b;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Problem statement&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="228" x="47" y="1930" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-28" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffff88;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;underatnd the impact, delay, resource allgnment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="199" x="65" y="1953" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-29" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#cdeb8b;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;get everyone onboard, what is required , software update or upgrade, patch, effrot&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="49" width="341" x="47" y="1991" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-30" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffff88;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;update RAID log&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="186" x="89" y="2049" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-31" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#cdeb8b;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;recover plan,&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;dedicate responsibility, owner, timeline, regression testing, performance and service impact, Stakeholders approval&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="112" width="329" x="57" y="2071" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-32" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffff88;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;manage the schedule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left; font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Look for activities that can runn in parallel, Site radines, test-case prep, documentation, configuration prep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="99" width="324.25" x="65" y="2194" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-33" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#cdeb8b;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Stk-hol , impact , aciton, owner, revised dates&lt;br&gt;just not esclated but with full view&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="321" x="67" y="2300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-34" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffff88;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;unexpected technical dependency into a controlled project action. We understood the impact, identified the required upgrade, managed the dependency and testing, and protected the overall delivery as much as possible.”&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="65" width="550" x="62.99553858478879" y="2342" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-35" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" value="&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;One example is from a 5G NSA launch project. During the &lt;b&gt;execution phase&lt;/b&gt;, while we were doing integrations and testing, we identified that the existing &lt;b&gt;CMG&lt;/b&gt; was not running on the software version required to support the dual-radio functionality needed for the planned deployment.&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;I first checked the &lt;b&gt;impact&lt;/b&gt; with the technical leads and vendor. We established that this was a blocker for the planned end-to-end testing and therefore represented a &lt;b&gt;risk&lt;/b&gt; to the project milestone.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;I captured it in the &lt;b&gt;RAID&lt;/b&gt; log, identified the &lt;b&gt;technical owner&lt;/b&gt; and worked with the &lt;b&gt;CMG&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;vendor&lt;/b&gt;, RAN, core (PCRF) and testing teams to understand the required upgrade path, dependencies, resources and testing effort.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;so instead of simply &lt;b&gt;moving the milestone&lt;/b&gt;, I try to develop a recovery plan. We planned the &lt;b&gt;CMG software upgrade&lt;/b&gt;, arranged the &lt;b&gt;required resources&lt;/b&gt; and change window, and identified which &lt;b&gt;project activities&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;those could continue in parallel while the upgrade was being prepared. &lt;b&gt;cisco bug sfp&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;After the upgrade, we completed the required &lt;b&gt;regression&lt;/b&gt; and 5G NSA integration testing and validated the dual-radio functionality. during all this I maintained regular &lt;b&gt;stakeholder communication&lt;/b&gt; throughout the process, including the &lt;b&gt;impact&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;actions&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;owners&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;revised timelines&lt;/b&gt;. my experience of stakholder&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The important thing from my &lt;b&gt;personal&amp;nbsp; perspective&lt;/b&gt; was that I didn&#39;t try to solve the technical issue myself as the Project Manager. My role was to &lt;b&gt;point fingers&lt;/b&gt; but make sure the right technical &lt;b&gt;teams were engaged&lt;/b&gt;, the dependency was &lt;b&gt;clearly owned&lt;/b&gt;, the &lt;b&gt;impact was understood&lt;/b&gt;, the &lt;b&gt;recovery plan was agreed&lt;/b&gt;, and the project remained &lt;b&gt;under control&lt;/b&gt;, and I convert unexpected technical dependency into a controlled project action&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The lesson I took from that experience was to validate software compatibility and critical technical dependencies as early as possible during project initiation and planning.”&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="409" width="943" x="12" y="2414" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vDpMT1KZrxu0gsrRI_nK-36" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" value="&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;When I create a project plan, I start with the project &lt;b&gt;objective&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;scope&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;key deliverables&lt;/b&gt;. Then I &lt;b&gt;break&lt;/b&gt; the project into &lt;b&gt;workstreams&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;activities&lt;/b&gt;, identify the &lt;b&gt;dependencies&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;owners&lt;/b&gt;, estimate the &lt;b&gt;duration&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;resources&lt;/b&gt; required, and sequence the activities to establish the critical path.&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;For example, for an HSS software upgrade, I would break it down into mobilisation, requirements and design, resource planning, software and environment readiness, change approval, deployment in the lab, integration, testing, defect resolution and retesting, production readiness, live deployment, ORT and handover.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;For each activity, I define who is responsible, what the dependency is, the planned start and finish date, and the required milestone or approval. I then identify risks, assumptions and issues and capture them in the RAID log.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Once the initial plan is created, I review it with the technical teams, vendor and key stakeholders to make sure the durations, dependencies and resources are realistic. After agreement, I baseline the plan.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;During execution, I track actual progress against the baseline, monitor the critical path, manage dependencies and changes, and update the plan when there is an approved change or a recovery action is required. I then report the overall status through regular project reporting.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="253.78" width="967.39" x="10" y="2857.22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
